# Artifacts

This directory contains intermediate files and supporting artifacts generated throughout the IEEE-CIS Fraud Detection project.

The artifacts are organized into five subdirectories corresponding to different stages of the machine learning workflow.

## Directory Structure

| Directory | Description |
|---|---|
| `artifacts_step0/` | Stores artifacts generated during initial project setup, data loading, preprocessing, and chronological train-validation splitting. |
| `artifacts_step1_eda/` | Stores outputs and supporting files generated during Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA). |
| `artifacts_step2_fe/` | Stores artifacts generated during feature engineering, including engineered features and related intermediate outputs. |
| `artifacts_step3_4_handover/` | Stores feature selection results and handover files prepared for subsequent modeling stages. |
| `artifacts_step5_model_inputs/` | Stores processed data and supporting files prepared as inputs for machine learning models. |

## Purpose

These directories preserve intermediate results from each stage of the project. They help organize the workflow, maintain consistency between processing stages, and support reproducibility.

## Reproducibility

The artifacts are generated by executing the corresponding stages of the project workflow in the main notebook:

`notebooks/IEEE_CIS_Project_END.ipynb`

**Note:** These files are intermediate project outputs rather than original dataset files. Some artifacts may be large and are therefore maintained separately from the public GitHub repository.
